    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. Using population covariance, the four sums of deviation products are respectively 28, -8, 22, and 4; dividing each by 4 gives 7, -2, 5.5, and 1. Taking logarithms in the four exponential equations gives x(1-log(7))=3, y(2ln(3)-1)=1, x(2ln(3)+6ln(8))=ln(8), and x(ln(4)+4ln(5))=8ln(5)-7ln(4). Factorial recurrence and cancellation give the six listed factorial answers, including the boundary cases using 0!=1. Secant has period 2\\pi and is even, so both secant expressions retain their given values. The q-73037 solution contains an authored prose error: it says to cancel k!, whereas its displayed calculation correctly cancels (k+1)!. Its final answer remains correct. The choices below use the exact current supplied values and option tokens.",
